KPL/SCLK

SYNTHETIC spacecraft clock kernel for spice-lite tests. This is not a real
mission clock and must never be used for anything but testing. It was written
by hand for test/sclk.test.mjs as the plainest clock that still needs more
than one linear piece: one partition and one coefficient record at a rate of
exactly one, running on TT (time system 2), so the only thing between the
clock and ET is the periodic TDB minus TT term.

Clock -903 has two fields: a count of nominal seconds and a count of 1/65536
second. Zero is at J2000 TT.

\begindata
SCLK_KERNEL_ID            = ( @2026-11-20T00:00:00 )
SCLK_DATA_TYPE_903        = ( 1 )
SCLK01_TIME_SYSTEM_903    = ( 2 )
SCLK01_N_FIELDS_903       = ( 2 )
SCLK01_MODULI_903         = ( 4294967296 65536 )
SCLK01_OFFSETS_903        = ( 0 0 )
SCLK01_OUTPUT_DELIM_903   = ( 1 )
SCLK_PARTITION_START_903  = ( 0.0000000000000E+00 )
SCLK_PARTITION_END_903    = ( 2.8147497671065E+14 )
SCLK01_COEFFICIENTS_903   = ( 0.0000000000000E+00  0.0000000000000E+00  1.0000000000000E+00 )
\begintext
